(text "11  -  SWD + UART HEADER" (at 259.0 107.4 0) (effects (font (size 2.3 2.3) (bold yes) (color 32 96 176 1)) (justify left)) (uuid "371b3650-207d-4f11-8144-f58fc8afdff9"))
(text_box "0R01 shunt x gain 100 = 1 V/A, so 3 A lands well inside the 3.3 V ADC span with no extra divider.  The 1k/10n pole rolls switching noise off ahead of both the ADC and the over-current comparator on sheet 1." (at 258 68 0) (size 68 20) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 0.95 0.95) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "8099544c-3ca0-4c69-9c5a-c393dc6abd83"))
(text_box "PNP Darlington pass device.  The op-amp sinks base current, so the stage needs no headroom above VOUT - an NPN follower would need a base drive above the output and runs out at the top of the range.  The shunt is high-side, between collector and VOUT, so the output negative stays at true ground and the INA181 reads correctly near 0 V." (at 82 30 0) (size 104 20) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "9bcc97ca-a8a1-4da7-ab8e-c86c734aafbc"))
(text_box "Grounding: one solid plane, not split between the switching and linear stages.  The two are in series, so they share a single return current; a slot would only force that current to detour and enlarge the loop.  Separate them by placement instead - keep each commutation loop tight, and star the analogue reference (divider bottoms, op-amp V-, INA181 REF, ADC GND) at the output cap negative." (at 134 108 0) (size 104 22) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "081ea71d-8f48-4099-b292-a20967ea7d1a"))
(text_box "STM32G030C8T6, chosen over the CH32V003 the prototype started on: that part has 18 GPIO and 17 were already committed, leaving nothing for the panel.  The G030 is the cheapest 48-pin Cortex-M0+ that is easy to source here and leaves ~18 pins spare.  Runs on the 16 MHz internal RC - no crystal, because nothing here needs better than 1 % timing.  SWD on PA13/PA14." (at 150 220 0) (size 71.39999999999999 25.88235294117647) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "fe538a36-52a3-4c6c-885c-e4f78583ae88"))
(text_box "Indicator LEDs sink rather than source: +3V3 - LED - R - GPIO, so a pin left tri-stated at reset cannot back-feed the rail.  PD_PG dark means the board fell back to a legacy 5 V port; SHDN_N lights on an over-current even with the MCU dead." (at 150 168 0) (size 44.199999999999996 25.88235294117647) (margins 0.9 0.9 0.9 0.9) (stroke (width 0) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 0.95 0.95) ) (justify left top)) (uuid "28573752-ad9e-4564-b902-c112759ced05"))
